WEBVTT

00:00:20.462 --> 00:00:22.022
Hello. I'm--

00:00:22.142 --> 00:00:25.462
-Dory!
-Dory! You're here.

00:00:25.622 --> 00:00:27.382
-Oh my baby!
-You're really here.

00:00:27.542 --> 00:00:28.582
-Let me look at you.
-You found us.

00:00:28.742 --> 00:00:30.902
-I'm never letting you go again.
-Oh my missing girl, you're here.

00:00:31.022 --> 00:00:32.062
-My baby!
-It's you.

00:00:32.262 --> 00:00:35.902
-Yes! Oh absolutely!
-It's really you! Mom, you're here.

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:38.742
-I am, I...
-And Dad, so are you.

00:00:38.822 --> 00:00:40.382
Right here, kelpcake.

00:00:43.942 --> 00:00:45.582
(CRYING) I'm so sorry.

00:00:45.742 --> 00:00:48.422
Oh honey. Oh honey, no. Kelpcake.

00:00:48.582 --> 00:00:52.262
I know I've got a problem. I know I'm--
And I'm so sorry.

00:00:52.422 --> 00:00:56.542
And all this time I've wanted to fix it
and I can't and I try. I try.

00:00:56.622 --> 00:00:59.422
But my thoughts-- they leave my head
and ideas change.

00:00:59.622 --> 00:01:01.742
And I'd forgotten you and I'm so sorry.

00:01:01.902 --> 00:01:06.942
Dory. Don't you dare be sorry.
Look what you did.

00:01:07.622 --> 00:01:10.782
-(SNIFFLES) What?
-You found us!

00:01:10.942 --> 00:01:12.702
That's right. You found us.

00:01:14.222 --> 00:01:17.662
Honey, why do you think
we stayed put here all these years?

00:01:17.822 --> 00:01:21.662
Because we believed one day
you'd find us again.

00:01:21.782 --> 00:01:22.982
Exactly!

00:01:23.662 --> 00:01:26.622
But I thought you were gone.
How did you--

00:01:26.702 --> 00:01:29.742
We went into quarantine
to look for you, but you weren't there.

00:01:29.942 --> 00:01:32.942
And we knew you must have
gotten out through the pipes.

00:01:33.102 --> 00:01:35.302
Through the pipes. That's right, sweetie.
And so we did too.

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:39.302
And we've stayed in this spot for you
ever since.

00:01:39.502 --> 00:01:41.822
-We thought you might come back.
-We stayed and waited for you.

00:01:41.982 --> 00:01:44.982
So every day, we go out and lay out...

00:01:45.942 --> 00:01:47.022
Shells.

00:01:52.502 --> 00:01:57.342
And you found us.
Oh honey, you found us.

00:01:57.502 --> 00:01:59.982
And you know why you found us?
Because you remembered.

00:02:01.542 --> 00:02:06.462
You remembered
in your own, amazing, Dory way.

00:02:07.502 --> 00:02:08.862
(SNIFFLES)

00:02:08.982 --> 00:02:11.862
I did. All by myself.

00:02:12.022 --> 00:02:17.502
Oh, honey. Really? Have you been
by yourself all these years?

00:02:17.702 --> 00:02:19.342
Oh, my poor little girl.

00:02:19.502 --> 00:02:23.342
Oh, I haven't been all by myself--
(GASPS) Marlin and Nemo!

00:02:24.302 --> 00:02:26.502
-Nobody saw where Dory went?
-ALL: No. Sorry. I didn't see anything.

00:02:26.662 --> 00:02:29.582
Seriously? That's a lot
of eyeballs doing nothing.

00:02:29.822 --> 00:02:31.422
Oh! Oh, excuse me. Can you help us?

00:02:31.582 --> 00:02:33.062
-We're looking--
-Me help you?

00:02:33.182 --> 00:02:34.142
(SNEEZES)

00:02:36.862 --> 00:02:38.702
NEMO: (GASPS) Dad, look! It's Dory.

00:02:38.822 --> 00:02:43.302
Oh, thank goodness. See, Nemo,
I knew she'd find a way-- What?

00:02:43.422 --> 00:02:44.822
Hey, where's Dory? Is she with you?

00:02:44.942 --> 00:02:47.022
(GASPS) I'm sorry.

00:02:47.102 --> 00:02:50.062
I tried to hold on,
but I couldn't and I lost her.

00:02:50.182 --> 00:02:52.142
-What?
-WOMAN: All right. Let's get going.

00:02:52.262 --> 00:02:53.422
No!

00:02:53.582 --> 00:02:56.102
DORY: And then the whale swallowed us
even though I speak whale.

00:02:56.182 --> 00:02:57.142
JENNY: A whale?

00:02:57.222 --> 00:02:58.342
CHARLIE: Good thing I wasn't
there to see that.

00:02:58.422 --> 00:03:00.342
DORY: Actually Marlin never believes
I even know how to speak whale...

00:03:00.542 --> 00:03:02.382
but you know what, he always kind of
trusts me anyway.

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:04.062
You know, I like this Marlin already.

00:03:04.222 --> 00:03:06.702
Yeah. And then somehow
we found Nemo. Or did he find me?

00:03:06.862 --> 00:03:09.262
I don't know. But, you know what,
Nemo is the sweetest.

00:03:09.462 --> 00:03:11.142
He just never gives up on me
no matter what.

00:03:11.222 --> 00:03:12.422
Um, what would Dory do?

00:03:12.582 --> 00:03:15.382
Well, we'll certainly have to thank
Marlin and Nemo when we meet them.

00:03:15.822 --> 00:03:16.822
(GRUNTS)

00:03:16.902 --> 00:03:19.102
Wait. Wait I know this place.

00:03:19.302 --> 00:03:22.302
SIGOURNEY ON SPEAKER:
Hello. I'm Sigourney Weaver.

00:03:22.422 --> 00:03:24.222
-There!
-Won't you please join us?

00:03:25.142 --> 00:03:28.262
-That's the Marine Life Institute.
-Oh, you were born there.

00:03:28.422 --> 00:03:29.262
Dory, is that where your friends are?

00:03:29.422 --> 00:03:33.462
Yes! They were stuck in something.
It was going somewhere.

00:03:33.542 --> 00:03:34.662
(TRUCK ENGINE STARTS)

00:03:34.782 --> 00:03:36.502
(GASPS) A truck. They're in the truck!

00:03:36.582 --> 00:03:38.622
That means I could--
Never see them again!

00:03:38.782 --> 00:03:40.822
No! No, no, no. What would Dory do?

00:03:41.782 --> 00:03:45.942
Uh, I know they're good friends of yours,
but a truck is kind of a tall order.

00:03:47.022 --> 00:03:49.262
Please! Please.
All I know is that I miss them. I-- I...

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:54.302
I really miss them.
I've said that before.

00:03:55.782 --> 00:03:56.782
Um...

00:03:56.902 --> 00:03:57.942
Dory?

00:03:58.062 --> 00:04:02.782
Mom, Marlin and Nemo are more
than good friends, they're family.

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:06.822
And I have to get them back.
See, when they found me it felt like fate.

00:04:06.942 --> 00:04:09.622
Do you know what I mean? Or... I don't--
What's another word for fate?

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:12.902
Like destiny. (GASPS) Destiny?

00:04:12.982 --> 00:04:14.862
(VOCALIZING) Destiny!

00:04:15.182 --> 00:04:17.102
-Dory?
-Destiny!

00:04:17.262 --> 00:04:20.502
-Morning, Dest--
-Sh. It's Dory. Something's wrong.

00:04:22.302 --> 00:04:25.662
(GASPS) Ooh. I got her.
She's right outside the institute.

00:04:26.102 --> 00:04:27.142
(DESTINY GROANS)

00:04:27.422 --> 00:04:28.622
-DORY: Destiny?
-We got to jump.

00:04:28.782 --> 00:04:30.382
-Jump?
-No time to argue!

00:04:30.502 --> 00:04:31.982
Destiny!

00:04:32.102 --> 00:04:34.982
Dory! The truck thing
with your friends is leaving!

00:04:35.142 --> 00:04:36.942
No, no. (VOCALIZING) Destiny.

00:04:37.022 --> 00:04:39.302
JENNY: Oh no! That's bad!
What do we do?

00:04:41.742 --> 00:04:42.822
-All right.
-Yes.

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:45.502
-Here we go. One. Two.
-Yes. Yes.

00:04:45.622 --> 00:04:47.502
I can't! I can't do it!
I'll never make it out there.

00:04:47.742 --> 00:04:51.182
Destiny! I've got the world's
most powerful pair of glasses.

00:04:51.342 --> 00:04:53.022
You've got the world's
most powerful pair of glasses.

00:04:53.182 --> 00:04:54.502
I will be your eyes.

00:04:54.662 --> 00:04:57.022
You can be my eyes. But the walls!

00:04:57.142 --> 00:04:59.222
There are no walls in the ocean!

00:04:59.862 --> 00:05:02.982
-No walls?
-(WHISPERS) It's your destiny, Destiny.

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:05.142
Well, why didn't you say so?

00:05:05.302 --> 00:05:08.662
What? No! Destiny, wait!
No, that's a wall! Wall!

00:05:08.742 --> 00:05:09.742
(SCREAMS)

00:05:10.182 --> 00:05:11.182
(ALL SCREAM)

00:05:14.022 --> 00:05:16.742
Mom, Dad, this is my pipe pal.
Destiny, say hi.

00:05:16.902 --> 00:05:18.782
Dory! Are these little blue blobs
your parents?

00:05:18.862 --> 00:05:20.222
They look just like you!

00:05:20.902 --> 00:05:23.542
Hello. I'm Bailey. Mrs. Dory, Mr. Dory.

00:05:23.702 --> 00:05:25.102
-Oh please, call me Jenny.
-Oh and I'm Charlie.

00:05:25.262 --> 00:05:27.102
Okay. Okay. We got to go.
We got to stop that truck.

00:05:27.702 --> 00:05:28.582
Okay, what truck?

00:05:30.062 --> 00:05:31.062
(DORY GASPS)

00:05:31.382 --> 00:05:32.702
Bailey, status report.

00:05:32.862 --> 00:05:36.062
Oh, yes, my beautiful gift. Ooh.

00:05:36.222 --> 00:05:38.382
Found it! The truck's merging
onto the freeway

00:05:38.462 --> 00:05:39.902
and it's heading south. Ooh.

00:05:40.062 --> 00:05:42.342
Let's go. We are stopping that truck.

00:05:43.782 --> 00:05:46.542
-This I've got to see.
-Yeah, yeah, me too!

00:05:47.222 --> 00:05:49.662
-Oh boy, this is gonna be good!
-(GERALD SNICKERS)

00:05:49.742 --> 00:05:52.182
What the-- Gerald!
Have you lost your marbles?

00:05:52.342 --> 00:05:54.862
-Don't get used to it, Gerald!
-Cheeky joke.

00:05:55.062 --> 00:05:56.382
(SNICKERING)

00:05:58.062 --> 00:05:59.942
Bailey, I forgot everything.
Catch me up.

00:06:00.102 --> 00:06:03.062
Yes, ma'am. Ooh.
Your friends are still on the truck.

00:06:03.262 --> 00:06:05.782
Ooh. They're headed north
towards the bridge. Ooh.

00:06:05.942 --> 00:06:08.302
Oh, look, there's a bunch of
cute otters over there.

00:06:08.422 --> 00:06:09.822
I want one! Ow!

00:06:09.902 --> 00:06:10.902
(SCREAMS)

00:06:13.182 --> 00:06:14.622
Ow, Bailey!

00:06:14.702 --> 00:06:16.782
Oh! I see the truck. It's over there.

00:06:16.982 --> 00:06:18.622
-Okay, what would Dory do?
-I don't see how we can get on it.

00:06:18.782 --> 00:06:20.822
Oh, man, if only there was a way
to stop traffic.

00:06:20.982 --> 00:06:23.542
Stop traffic. Stop traffic!
Everyone needs to stop.

00:06:23.742 --> 00:06:24.702
People stop to look at things.

00:06:24.782 --> 00:06:25.902
Things that they like.
Things that are cute.

00:06:26.382 --> 00:06:29.342
(GASPS) Things that are cute!
Okay, I got it.

00:06:29.422 --> 00:06:31.142
-What? What is it?
-Quickly before I forget.

00:06:31.302 --> 00:06:33.942
Destiny, when the truck reaches
the bridge you flip me up there.

00:06:34.102 --> 00:06:34.702
Got it.

00:06:34.822 --> 00:06:37.622
You guys, follow me.
Everyone else, stay here.

00:06:37.782 --> 00:06:41.342
Whoa. Dory.
Honey, you're not leaving us again.

00:06:41.502 --> 00:06:43.182
Your mother's right.
You have to stay with us.

00:06:43.342 --> 00:06:47.182
Dory, what happens if--
You know, if you're gone for too long.

00:06:47.342 --> 00:06:50.062
And what if you get confused and that
makes you distracted. And what if--

00:06:50.182 --> 00:06:51.462
I lose you again?

00:06:52.342 --> 00:06:54.102
Oh. Yes.

00:06:55.542 --> 00:06:58.342
Mom, Dad,
it's gonna be okay because...

00:06:58.502 --> 00:07:02.302
I know that even if I forget
I can find you again.

